cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Medical Report Information Extractor: on-premises LLM extraction of structured data from pathology reports and discharge summaries"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shokun
    given-names: Nazarii
    affiliation: "University of Salento, Lecce, Italy"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nazarshokun/medical_report_information_extractor"
abstract: >-
  A Streamlit application for extracting structured data from free-text
  medical documents (pathology reports and discharge summaries) with large
  language models. Extraction tasks are defined by configurable JSON Schemas
  and instructions. For patient data, it runs entirely on-premises with local
  open-weight models (Ollama, LM Studio or other OpenAI-compatible servers) and
  on-device OCR for scanned PDFs, so no document text leaves the hospital.
  It supports lymphoma registries by pre-filling REDCap registration forms for
  data-manager verification.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - information extraction
  - pathology reports
  - discharge summaries
  - lymphoma
  - clinical registries
  - REDCap
  - OCR
  - privacy-preserving
